cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Graph memory: a false catalog claim"
message: "If you use this experiment, its results, or its records, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ramona C."
    family-names: Truta
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-4886-7777"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rctruta/nodes26"
url: "https://github.com/rctruta/nodes26"
abstract: >-
  A controlled, reproducible case study of one graph-backed agent-memory
  pipeline. A fictional catalog entry describes a nonexistent lamp. The
  experiment asks whether the official extractor persists it as a typed entity,
  whether a later semantic search retrieves it, and whether a fresh agent uses
  it in an answer.
keywords:
  - agent-memory
  - knowledge-graph
  - Neo4j
  - memory-poisoning
  - reproducibility
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-11"
